<!-- CHAPTER 4: SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>4. Software Requirements Specification (SRS)</h1>

<h2>4.1 Functional Requirements</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>FR-1: User Authentication &amp; Profile Management:</strong> Secure registration/login using BCrypt (work factor 12) and JWT. Supports 7 route preferences (<code>STANDARD</code>, <code>FASTEST</code>, <code>BALANCED</code>, <code>SAFEST</code>, <code>SOLO_TRAVELLER</code>, <code>TOURIST</code>, <code>ELDERLY</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>FR-2: Multi-Objective Pedestrian Routing:</strong> Calculates optimal walking paths balancing transit time, distance, and ML-predicted relative risk.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-3: Dynamic Route Comparison &amp; Trade-off Synthesis:</strong> Returns 3 simultaneous routes (<code>FASTEST</code>, <code>BALANCED</code>, <code>SAFEST</code>) detailing time deltas, distance deltas, and safety improvement percentage.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-4: Street-Level Safety Heatmap:</strong> Bounding-box queries (&le; 0.15&deg; span) returning road segments colored by safety tier, with neutral dashed lines for unscored segments.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-5: Safe Zones Directory:</strong> PostGIS spatial queries (<code>ST_DWithin</code>) for police stations, hospitals, pharmacies, and transit stations without authentication.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-6: Community Safety Reporting:</strong> Report submission with optional GPS consent, asynchronous moderation lifecycle (<code>PENDING</code> &rarr; <code>VERIFIED</code> / <code>REJECTED</code>), PII scrubbing, and sliding-window rate limiting.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-7: Emergency SOS &amp; Helpline Integration:</strong> Cap of 5 trusted contacts, immutable audit logging on SOS trigger, and native telephony dialers for 112, 100, 108, 1091.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-8: Ambient Weather Observation:</strong> Hourly weather data fetched from Open-Meteo with ~1.1 km quantized grid caching.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 Non-Functional Requirements</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>NFR-1: Performance &amp; Latency:</strong> Route calculation under 500 ms; batch ML inference under 250 ms.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-2: Security &amp; Privacy:</strong> OWASP Top 10 API Security compliance, BCrypt password hashing, role-based access control (USER, MODERATOR, ADMIN), input bean validation, and sanitized error responses.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-3: Reliability &amp; Graceful Degradation:</strong> Deterministic routing fallbacks if ML service or weather API is offline.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-4: Data Integrity:</strong> Strict coordinate boundaries [-90, 90] and [-180, 180]; zero invented crime data.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-5: Client Usability:</strong> Interactive touch zoom/pan maps without proprietary billing keys.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 5: SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & ENGINEERING DESIGN -->
